hadiths[354]{hadithnumber,text}:
3605,"Narrated Wathilah bin Al-Asqa':that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed Allah has chosen Isma'il from the children of Ibrahim"
3606,"Narrated Wathilah bin Al-Asqa':that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed"
3607,"Narrated Al-'Abbas bin 'Abdul-Muttalib:""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Indeed the Quraish have sat and spoken between themselves about the best of them"
3608,"Narrated Al-Muttalib bin Abi Wada'ah:""Al-Abbas came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
3609,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:""They said: 'O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)! When was the Prophethood established for you?' He said: 'While Adam was between (being) soul and body"
3610,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""I am the first of the people to appear upon their being resurrected"
3611,"Narrated Abu Hurairah [may Allah be pleased with him]:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""I am the first for whom the earth will be split"
3612,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Ask Allah to grant me Al-Wasilah."" They said: ""O Messenger of Allah! And what is Al-Wasilah?"" He said: ""The highest level of Paradise. No one will attain it except for one man"
3613,"Narrated At-Tufail bin Ubayy bin Ka'b:from his father that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The parable of me and the Prophets is that of a man who built a house"
3614,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amr:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""If you hear the Muadh-dhin then say as he says. Then send Salat upon me"
3615,"Narrated Abu Sa'eed:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""I am the master of the children of Adam on the Day of Judgement"
3616,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that a group of people from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sat waiting for him. He said: ""Then he came out"
3617,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin Salam:""The description of Muhammad is written in the Tawrah"
3618,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:""On the day in which the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered Al-Madinah"
3619,Narrated Al-Muttalib bin 'Abdullah bin Qais bin Makhramah:from his father
3620,"Narrated Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari:""Abu Talib departed to Ash-Sham"
3621,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) received Revelation when he was forty years old. So he stayed in Makkah for thirteen years and in Al-Madinah for ten. And he died when he was sixty-three years old"
3622,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""The Prophet (ﷺ) died when he was sixty-five years old"
3623,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was not very tall nor was he [very] short"
3624,Narrated Simak bin Harb:from Jabir bin Samurah
3625,"Narrated Abu Al-'Ala:from Samurah bin Jundab that he said: ""We were with the Prophet (ﷺ) and we would take turns (eating) from a bowl from the morning till the evening. Ten would stand and ten would sit."" We said: ""So what was filling it up?' He said: ""What are you amazed at? It wasn't filled up from anywhere but here"
3626,"Narrated 'Ali bin Abi Talib:""I was with the Prophet (ﷺ) in Makkah. We departed to one of its suburbs"
3627,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to give Khutbah next to a tree"
3628,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""A Bedouin came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: 'How shall I know that you are a Prophet?' He said: 'If I were to call this date cluster from this palm tree"
3629,"Narrated Abu Zaid bin Akhtab:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) wiped his hand over my face and supplicated for me."" 'Azrah (one of the narrators) said: ""Indeed he lived for one-hundred and twenty years"
3630,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:""Abu Talhah said to Umm Sulaim: 'I heard the voice of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sounding weak and I sensed some hunger in it. Do you have anything? She said: 'Yes.' So she got some loaves of wheat bread"
3631,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:""I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) at the time when the 'Asr prayer had drawn near"
3632,"Narrated 'Aishah:""The first of what the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) initiated with of Prophethood"
3633,"Narrated 'Abdullah:""You consider the signs to be punishment"
3634,Narrated 'Aishah:that Al-Harith bin Hisham asked the Prophet (ﷺ): 'How does the Revelation come to you?' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Sometimes it comes to me like the ringing of a bell and that is the hardest upon me
3635,"Narrated Al-Bara:""I have not seen anyone with hair past his shoulders in a red Hullah more handsome than the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He had hair that would flow on his shoulders"
3636,"Narrated Abu Ishaq:""A man asked Al-Bara: 'Was the face of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) like a sword?' He said: 'No"
3637,"Narrated 'Ali:""The Prophet (ﷺ) was not tall nor was he short"
3638,Narrated Ibrahim bin Muhammad
3639,"Narrated 'Urwah:that 'Aishah said: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not speak quickly like you do now"
3640,Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would repeat a statement three times so that it could be understood
3641,"Narrated Ibn Jaz:""I have not seen anyone who smiled more than the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
3642,"Narrated Ibn Jaz:""The laughter of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was not but smiling"
3643,"Narrated As-Sa'ib bin Yazid:""My maternal aunt took me to the Prophet (ﷺ)"
3644,"Narrated Jabir bin Samurah:""The seal of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"" - meaning the one which was between his two shoulder blades - ""was fleshy and red"
3645,"Narrated Jabir bin Samurah:""The two shins of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) were thin"
3646,"Narrated Jabir bin Samurah:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had a wide mouth (Dali' Al-Fam)"
3647,"Narrated Jabir bin Samurah:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) had a wide mouth (Dali' Al-Fam)"
3648,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:""I have not seen anything more beautiful than the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). It was as if the sun flowed upon his face. And I have not seen anyone quicker in his walking than the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). It was as if the earth was made easy for him. We would be exerting ourselves while he would not be struggling"
3649,"Narrated Jabir:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The Prophets were presented to me"
3650,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""The Prophet (ﷺ) died when he was sixty-five years old"
3651,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""The Prophet (ﷺ) died when he was sixty-five years old"
3652,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""The Prophet (ﷺ) stayed in Makkah for thirteen years - meaning while he was receiving Revelation - and he died when he was sixty-three years old"
3653,Narrated Jabir [bin 'Abdullah]:that he heard Mu'awiyah bin Abi Sufyan giving a Khutbah
3654,"Narrated 'Aishah [may Allah be pleased with her]:""The Prophet (ﷺ) died when he was sixty-three years old"
3655,"Narrated 'Abdullah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""I free myself of the friendship of every Khalil"
3656,"Narrated 'Umar bin Al-Khattab:""Abu Bakr is our chief"
3657,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin Shaqiq:""I said to 'Aishah: 'Which of the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) were the most beloved to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?' She said: 'Abu Bakr.' I said: 'Then who?' She said: ''Umar.' I said: ""Then who?' She said: 'Then Abu 'Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah.'"" He said: ""I said: 'Then who?''"" He said: ""Then she was silent"
3658,"Narrated Abu Sa'eed:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed the people of the higher levels"
3659,"Narrated Ibn Abi Mu'alla:from his father: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave a Khutbah one day and said: 'Indeed there is a man whose Lord has given him the choice between living in this life as long as he wishes to live"
3660,"Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sat upon the Minbar and said: 'Indeed a worshiper has been given a choice by Allah"
3661,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""There is no favor due upon us from anyone"
3662,"Narrated Hudhaifah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Stick to the two after me"
3663,"Narrated Hudhaifah [may Allah be pleased with him]:""We were sitting with the Prophet (ﷺ) and he said: 'I do not know how long I will be with you"
3664,"Narrated Anas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said about Abu Bakr and 'Umar: ""These two are the masters of the elder people among the inhabitants of Paradise. From the first ones and the last ones"
3665,"Narrated 'Ali bin Abi Talib:""I was with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
3666,"Narrated 'Ali:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Abu Bakr and 'Umar are the masters of the elder people among the inhabitants of Paradise"
3667,"Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri:that Abu Bakr said: ""Am I not the most deserving of it among the people"
3668,Narrated Anas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to go out to his Companions from The Muhajirin and the Ansar while they were sitting
3669,Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) departed one day and entered the Masjid
3670,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to Abu Bakr: ""You are my companion at the Hawd"
3671,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin Hantab:that the Prophet (ﷺ) saw Abu Bakr and 'Umar and said: ""These two are the hearing and the seeing"
3672,"Narrated 'Aishah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Order Abu Bakr to lead the people in Salat."" 'Aishah said: ""O Messenger of Allah! If Abu Bakr takes your place"
3673,"Narrated 'Aishah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""It is not befitting that a group"
3674,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever spends a pair of things in the path of Allah"
3675,"Narrated Zaid bin Aslam:""I heard 'Umar bin Al-Khattab saying: 'We were ordered by the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to give in charity"
3676,Narrated Jubair bin Mut'im:that a woman came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to speak to him about something. Then he ordered her with something
3677,Narrated Abu Salamah bin 'Abdur-Rahman:from Abu Hurairah
3678,Narrated 'Aishah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) ordered the closing of all the gates
3679,Narrated 'Aishah:that Abu Bakr entered upon the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)
3680,"Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""There is no Prophet except that he has two ministers among the inhabitants of the heavens"
3681,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""O Allah! Honor Islam through the most dear of these two men to you: Through Abu Jahl or through 'Umar bin Al-Khattab."" He said: ""And the most dear of them to Him was 'Umar"
3682,Narrated Nafi':from Ibn 'Umar
3683,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""O Allah honor Islam through Abu Jahl bin Hisham or through 'Umar bin Al-Khattab."" He said: ""So it happened that 'Umar came the next day to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and accepted Islam"
3684,"Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:that 'Umar said to Abu Bakr: ""O best of people after the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)!"" So Abu Bakr said: ""If you say that"
3685,"Narrated Muhammad bin Sirin:""I don't think that a man who degrades Abu Bakr and 'Umar loves the Prophet (ﷺ)"
3686,"Narrated 'Uqbah bin 'Amir:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""If there was to have a Prophet after me"
3687,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'I saw that I was brought a cup of milk"
3688,"Narrated Anas:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""I entered Paradise and it was as if I was in a palace of gold. So I said: 'Whose palace is this?' They said: 'A youth's"
3689,"Narrated Abu Buraidah:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) awoke in the morning and called for Bilal"
3690,"Narrated Buraidah:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) went out for one of his expeditions"
3691,Narrated 'Aishah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was sitting and we heard a scream and the voices of children. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) arose
3692,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""I am the first for whom the earth will split"
3693,"Narrated 'Aishah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Among the nations"
3694,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""A man among the inhabitants of Paradise will appear before you."" So Abu Bakr appeared. Then he said: ""A man among the inhabitants of Paradise will appear before you."" So 'Umar appeared"
3695,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""While a man was tending some of his sheep"
3696,Narrated Abu Hurairah [may Allah be pleased with him]:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was at Hira
3697,Narrated Anas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)
3698,"Narrated Talhah bin 'Ubaidullah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""For every Prophet there is a friend (Rafiq)"
3699,"Narrated Abu 'Abdur-Rahman As-Sulami:""When 'Uthman was besieged"
3700,"Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin Khabbab:""I witnessed the Prophet (ﷺ) while he was exhorting support for the 'army of distress.' 'Uthman bin 'Affan stood and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! I will take the responsibility of one-hundred camels"
3701,"Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin Samurah:that 'Uthman went to the Prophet (ﷺ) with one-thousand Dinar"" - Al-Hasan bin Waqi (one of the narrators) said: ""And in another place in my book: 'In his garment when the 'army of distress' was being prepared. So he poured them into his lap.'"" - 'Abdur-Rahman said: ""So I saw the Prophet (ﷺ) turning them over in his lap"
3702,Narrated Anas bin Malik:that when the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered the pledge of Ridwan
3703,"Narrated Thumamah bin Hazn Al-Qushairi:""I was present at the house when 'Uthman appeared above them saying: 'Bring me your two companions who have gathered you against me.'"" He said: ""So they were brought as if they were two camels"
3704,"Narrated Abu Al-Ash'ath As-Sana'ani:""Some people were delivering Khutbah in Ash-Sham"
3705,"Narrated 'Aishah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""O 'Uthman! Indeed Allah may give you a shirt"
3706,"Narrated 'Uthman bin 'Abdullah bin Mawhab:""A man among the people of Egypt performed Hajj to the House"
3707,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:""While the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was alive"
3708,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) mentioned the Fitnah and said: ""This one will be wrongfully killed during it"
3709,Narrated Jabir:that the Prophet (ﷺ) was brought the body of a deceased man
3710,"Narrated Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari:""I went with the Prophet (ﷺ) and he entered a garden of the Ansar"
3711,"Narrated Abu Sahlah:""The day of the house (when he was besieged)"
3712,Narrated 'Imran bin Husain:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) dispatched an army and he put 'Ali bin Abi Talib in charge of it. He left on the expedition and he entered upon a female slave. So four of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) scolded him
3713,Narrated Abu Sarihah
3714,"Narrated 'Ali bin Abi Talib:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""May Allah have mercy upon Abu Bakr"
3715,"Narrated Rib'i bin Hirash:""At Ar-Rahbah"
3716,"Narrated Al-Bara bin 'Azib:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said to 'Ali bin Abi Talib: ""You are from me"
3717,Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri:\n
\n  We," the people of the Ansar, used to recognize the hypocrites, by their hatred for 'Ali bin Abi Talib. \nJam e Tirmazi Hadees: 3717 Arabic Hadees: 3717"""
3718,"Narrated Buraidah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed Allah has ordered me to love four"
3719,"Narrated Hubshi bin Junadah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""'Ali is from me and I am from 'Ali. And none should represent me except myself or 'Ali"
3720,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) made bonds of brotherhood among his Companions. So 'Ali came crying saying: ""O Messenger of Allah! You have made a bond of brotherhood among your Companions"
3721,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:""There was a bird with the Prophet (ﷺ)"
3722,"Narrated 'Ali:""When I would ask the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
3723,"Narrated 'Ali:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""I am the house of wisdom"
3724,Narrated 'Amir bin Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas:from his father
3725,"Narrated Al-Bara:""The Prophet (ﷺ) dispatched two armies and put 'Ali bin Abi Talib in charge of one of them"
3726,"Narrated Jabir:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) called 'Ali on the Day (of the battle) of At-Ta'if"
3727,"Narrated Abu Sa'eed:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to 'Ali: ""O 'Ali! It is not permissible for anyone to be Junub in this Masjid except for you and I"
3728,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:""The advent of the Prophet (ﷺ) was on Monday and 'Ali performed Salat on Tuesday"
3729,"Narrated Ali:""When I would ask the Messenger of Allah SAW he would give me"
3730,"Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said to 'Ali: ""You are to me in the position that Harun was to Musa"
3731,Narrated Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said to 'Ali
3732,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""The Prophet (ﷺ) ordered that the gates be closed"
3733,Narrated 'Ali bin Husain:from his father
3734,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""The first to perform Salat was 'Ali"
3735,"Narrated a man from the Ansar:that Zaid bin Al-Arqam said: ""The first to accept Islam was 'Ali."" 'Amr bin Murrah said: ""So I mentioned that to Ibrahim An-Nakha'i"
3736,"Narrated 'Ali:""The Prophet (ﷺ) - the Unlettered Prophet - exhorted me (saying): 'None loves you except a believer and none hates you except a hypocrite.'"" 'Adi bin Thabit (a narrator) said: ""I am from the generation whom the Prophet (ﷺ) supplicated for"
3737,"Narrated Umm 'Atiyyah:""The Prophet (ﷺ) sent an army in which was 'Ali."" She said: ""While he was raising his hands"
3738,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin Az-Zubair:that Az-Zubair said: ""On the Day of (the battle of) Uhud"
3739,"Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever would be pleased to look at a martyr walking upon the face of the earth"
3740,"Narrated Musa bin Talhah:""I entered upon Mu'awiyah and he said: 'Shall I not give you some good news?' I said: 'Of course!' He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: 'Talhah is among those who fulfilled their vow (referring to 33:)"
3741,"Narrated 'Ali bin abi Talib:""My ear heard from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
3742,Narrated Musa and 'Eisa
3743,Narrated 'Abdullah bin Az-Zubair:from Az-Zubair
3744,"Narrated 'Ali bin Abi Talib [may Allah be pleased with him]:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed"
3745,"Narrated Jabir [may Allah be pleased with him]:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed"
3746,"Narrated Hisham bin 'Urwah:""On the Day of (the battle of) Al-Jamal"
3747,"Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin 'Awf:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Abu Bakr is in Paradise"
3748,Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin Humaid:from his father
3749,"Narrated Abu Salamah:from 'Aishah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to say: ""Indeed your affair [feminine plural: referring to the wives of the Prophet (ﷺ)] is from that which concerns me after me"
3750,Narrated Abu Salamah:that 'Abdur-Rahman bin 'Awf left a garden for the Mothers of the Believers that was sold for four-hundred thousand
3751,"Narrated Sa'd:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""O Allah"
3752,"Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:""Sa'd came"
3753,"Narrated 'Ali:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not mention both (his) parents for anyone except Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas. On the Day of (the battle of) Uhud he said: 'Shoot"
3754,"Narrated Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) mentioned both of his parents for me on the Day of Uhud"
3755,"Narrated 'Ali bin Abi Talib:""I never heard the Prophet (ﷺ) mentioning both of his parents being ransomed for anyone except for Sa'd. On the Day of Uhud"
3756,"Narrated 'Aishah:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not sleep one night upon arriving in Al-Madinah. So he said: 'If only a righteous man would guard me tonight.'"" She said: ""So we were like that"
3757,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin Zalim Al-Mazini:that Sa'eed bin Zaid bin 'Amr bin Nufail said: ""I bear witness for nine people"
3758,Narrated 'Abdul-Muttalib bin Rabi'ah bin Al-Harith bin 'Abdul-Muttalib:\n
\n  Al-'Abbas bin 'Abdul-Muttalib entered upon the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in a state of anger while I was with him," so he said: 'What has angered you?' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what is it with us and the Quraish, whenever they meet one another it is with glad faces, and when they meet us they meet us with other than that?'   He said:   So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) became angry, until his face reddened, then he said: 'By the One in Whose Hand is my soul! Faith does not enter a man's heart until he loves you for the sake of Allah, and for the sake of His Messenger.' Then he said: 'O people! Whoever harms my uncle, he has harmed me, for indeed, a man's uncle is not but the Sinw (two or three palm trees will come from a single root, so each is called a Sinw. A man's uncle is like that to his father. That is, he is like his father) of his father. \nJam e Tirmazi Hadees: 3758 Arabic Hadees: 3758"""
3759,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\n\nthat the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:   Al-'Abbas is from me and I am from him. \nJam e Tirmazi Hadees: 3759 Arabic Hadees: 3759"""
3760,Narrated 'Ali:that concerning Al-'Abbas
3761,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Al-'Abbas is the uncle of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
3762,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to Al-'Abbas: 'On the night of Monday"
3763,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""I saw Ja'far flying in Paradise with the angels"
3764,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:""None has put on sandals - nor worn them"
3765,"Narrated Al-Bara bin 'Azib:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said to Ja'far bin Abi Talib: ""You share similarity with me in appearance and in character"
3766,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:""I used to ask a man from among the Companions of the Prophet (ﷺ) concerning Ayat of the Qur'an which I would be more knowledgeable about than him"
3767,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:""We used to call Ja'far bin Abi Talib the Father of the Poor"
3768,"Narrated Abu Sa'eed:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Al-Hasan and Al-Husain are the chiefs of the youths of Paradise"
3769,"Narrated Usamah bin Zaid:""I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) one night concerning some need"
3770,"Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin Abu Nu'm:that a man from the people of Al-'Iraq asked Ibn 'Umar about the blood of a gnat that gets on the clothes. Ibn 'Umar said ""Look at this one"
3771,"Narrated Salma:""I entered upon Umm Salamah while she was crying"
3772,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was asked: ""Which of the people of your house are most beloved to you?"" He said: ""Al-Hasan and Al-Husain."" And he used to say to Fatimah: ""Call my two sons for me so that I may smell them."" And he would hug them"
3773,"Narrated Abu Bakrah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ascended the Minbar and said: ""Indeed"
3774,"Narrated Buraidah:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was delivering a Khutbah to us when Al-Hasan and Al-Husain [peace be upon them] came"
3775,"Narrated Ya'la bin Murrah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Husain is from me"
3776,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:""None of them used to resemble the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) more than Al-Hasan bin 'Ali"
3777,"Narrated Abu Juhaifah:""I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
3778,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:""I was with Ibn Ziyad and the head of Al-Husain was brought. He began to poke it in the nose with a stick that he had"
3779,"Narrated 'Ali:said: ""Al-Hasan is greater in resemblance to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) with regards to what is between the chest and the head"
3780,"Narrated 'Umarah bin 'Umair:""When the heads of 'Ubaidullah bin Ziyad and his companions were brought"
3781,"Narrated Hudhaifah :""My mother asked me: 'When is your planned time - meaning with the Prophet (ﷺ)?' So I said: 'I have not had a planned time to see him since such and such time.' She rebuked me"
3782,Narrated Al-Bara:that the Prophet (ﷺ) saw Hasan and Husain
3783,"Narrated Al-Bara bin 'Azib:""I saw the Prophet (ﷺ) placing Al-Hasan bin 'Ali upon his shoulder while saying: 'O Allah"
3784,Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was carrying Al-Hasan bin 'Ali upon his shoulder
3785,"Narrated Al-Musayyab bin Najabah:""'Ali bin Abi Talib said: 'The Prophet SAW said: ""Indeed every Prophet is given seven select attendants"" - or he said: ""guards"" - ""and I was given fourteen."" We said: ""Who are they?"" He said: 'Myself"
3786,"Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:""I saw the Messenger of Allah during his Hajj"
3787,"Narrated 'Umar bin Abi Salamah - the step-son of the Prophet (ﷺ):""When these Ayat were revealed to the Prophet (ﷺ): 'Allah only wishes to remove the Rijs from you"
3788,Narrated Zaid bin Arqam
3789,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Love Allah for what He nourishes you with of His Blessings"
3790,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The most merciful of my nation to my nation is Abu Bakr"
3791,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The most merciful of my nation to my nation is Abu Bakr"
3792,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to Ubayy bin Ka'b: ""Indeed Allah ordered me to recite to you: Those who disbelieve were not going to... (98:1) He said: ""And He named me?"" He said: ""Yes."" So he wept"
3793,"Narrated Ubayy bin Ka'b:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to him: ""Indeed"
3794,"Narrated Qatadah:that Anas bin Malik said: ""Four gathered the Qur'an during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
3795,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""What an excellent man is Abu Bakr"
3796,"Narrated Hudhaifah bin Al-Yaman:that Al-'Aqib and As-Sayyid (two of the leaders of the Christians of Najran) came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and said: ""Send with us your trustworthy one."" He said: ""I shall send with you a trustworthy one who is truly a trustworthy one."" So the people desired that"
3797,Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Indeed
3798,Narrated 'Ali:that 'Ammar bin Yasir came seeking permission to enter upon the Prophet (ﷺ) so he said: 'Permit him
3799,Narrated 'Aishah:\n
\nthat the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said:   Ammar is not given a choice between two matters," except that he choose the one with more guidance in it. \nJam e Tirmazi Hadees: 3799 Arabic Hadees: 3799"""
3800,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Rejoice"
3801,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amr:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""There is no one more truthful"
3802,"Narrated Abu Dharr:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""There is no one more truthful in speech"
3803,"Narrated 'Abdul-Malik bin 'Umair:from the nephew of 'Abdullah bin Salam who said: ""When they were about to kill 'Uthman"
3804,"Narrated Yazid bin 'Umairah:""When death was upon Mu'adh bin Jabal"
3805,"Narrated Ibn Mas'ud:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Take as examples the two after me from my Companions"
3806,"Narrated Abu Musa:""My brother and I arrived from Yemen"
3807,"Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin Yazid:""We came to Hudhaifah and said: 'Inform us of the closest to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) in guidance and conduct"
3808,"Narrated 'Ali:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""If I was going to appoint anyone of them as a leader without any consultation"
3809,"Narrated 'Ali:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""If I was going to appoint anyone as a leader without any consultation"
3810,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Amr:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Take the Qur'an from four: From Ibn Mas'ud"
3811,"Narrated Khaithamah bin Abi Sabrah:""I came to Al-Madinah"
3812,"Narrated Hudhaifah:that they said: ""O Messenger of Allah"
3813,Narrated Zaid bin Aslam:from his father
3814,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:""We called Zaid bin Harithah nothing but 'Zaid bin Muhammad' until the Qur'an was revealed (ordering): Call them by their fathers"
3815,Narrated Jabalah bin Harithah
3816,Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent and army and put Usamah bin Zaid in charge of them. So the people contested his leadership
3817,Narrated Muhammad bin Usamah bin Zaid:from his father
3818,Narrated 'Aishah
3819,"Narrated Usamah bin Zaid:""I was sitting [with the Prophet (ﷺ)] when 'Ali and Al-'Abbas came seeking permission to enter. They said: 'O Usamah"
3820,"Narrated Jarir bin 'Abdullah:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) never screened me since I accepted Islam"
3821,"Narrated Jarir:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) never screened me since I accepted Islam"
3822,Narrated Abu Jahdam:from Ibn 'Abbas that he saw Jibra'il (AS)
3823,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) supplicated for me that Allah should give me Al-Hukm (knowledge"
3824,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) pulled me close to him and said: 'O Allah"
3825,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:""I had a dream in which I saw as if there was a piece of silk in my hand"
3826,Narrated Ibn Abi Mulaikah:from 'Aishah
3827,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) passed by"
3828,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said to him: ""O possessor of two ears!"" (One of the narrators) Abu Usamah said: 'He only meant it as a joke"
3829,Narrated Anas bin Malik:from Umm Sulaim
3830,"Narrated Anas [may Allah be pleased with him]:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave me my Kunyah because of a plant that I used to care for"
3831,"Narrated Thabit Al-Bunani:""Anas bin Malik said to me: 'O Thabit"
3832,Narrated Thabit:from Anas
3833,"Narrated Abu Khaldah:""I said to Abu Al-'Aliyah: '(Did) Anas heard from the Prophet (ﷺ)?' He said: 'He served him for ten years"
3834,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:""I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) and spread out my garment next to him"
3835,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah"
3836,"Narrated Al-Walid bin 'Abdur-Rahman:that Ibn 'Umar said to Abu Hurairah: ""You used to stick to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) most out of all of us"
3837,"Narrated Malik bin Abi 'Amir:""A man came to Talhah bin 'Ubaidullah and said: 'O Abu Muhammad"
3838,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:""The Prophet (ﷺ) said to me: 'Who are you from?' I said: 'From Daws.' He said: 'I did not used think there was anyone from Daws in whom there was good"
3839,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:""I came to the Prophet (ﷺ) with some dates and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"
3840,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin Rafi':""I said to Abu Hurairah: 'Why were you given the Kunyah Abu Hurairah?' He said: 'Do you not fear me?'"" He said: ""Indeed"
3841,"Narrated Abu Hurairah [may Allah be pleased with him] :""There is none with more Ahadith from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) than I"
3842,Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin Abu 'Umairah - and he was one of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ):from the Prophet (ﷺ)
3843,"Narrated Abu Idris Al-Khawlani:""When 'Umar bin Al-Khattab removed 'Umair bin Sa'd as governor of Hims"
3844,"Narrated 'Uqbah bin 'Amir:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The people submitted while 'Amr bin Al-'As believed"
3845,"Narrated Talhah bin 'Ubaidullah:""I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: 'Indeed"
3846,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:""We camped with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) at a place"
3847,"Narrated Al-Bara:""A garment of silk was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) so they began to marvel at its softness"
3848,"Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:""I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
3849,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:""When the funeral of Sa'd bin Mu'adh was carried"
3850,"Narrated Anas:""Qais bin Sa'd used to be"
3851,"Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came to me"
3852,"Narrated Jabir:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) supplicated for forgiveness for me on the Night of the Camel"
3853,"Narrated Khabbab:""We emigrated with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
3854,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""How many are there with dishevelled hair"
3855,"Narrated Abu Musa:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""O Abu Musa! You have been given a Mizmar among the Mazamir of the family of Dawud"
3856,"Narrated Sahl bin Sa'd:""We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) while he was excavating the trench"
3857,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would say: ""O Allah! There is no life but the life of the Hereafter! So honor the Ansar and the Emigrants"
3858,"Narrated Talhah bin Khirash:""I heard Jabir bin 'Abdullah saying: 'I heard the Prophet (ﷺ) saying: ""The Fire shall not touch the Muslim who saw me"
3859,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The best generation is my generation"
3860,"Narrated Jabir:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""None of those who gave the pledge under the tree shall enter the Fire"
3861,"Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Do not abuse my Companions"
3862,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin Mughaffal:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""(Fear) Allah! (Fear) Allah regarding my Companions! Do not make them objects of insults after me. Whoever loves them"
3863,Narrated Abu Az-Zubair:from Jabir
3864,Narrated Abu Az-Zubair:from Jabir
3865,Narrated 'Abdullah bin Buraidah:from his father
3866,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""If you see those who abuse my Companions"
3867,"Narrated Al-Miswar bin Makhramah:""While he was on the Minbar"
3868,"Narrated Buraidah:""The most beloved of women to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was Fatimah and from the men was 'Ali"
3869,Narrated 'Abdullah bin Az-Zubair:that 'Ali mentioned the daughter of Abu Jahl (for marriage)
3870,Narrated Zaid bin Arqam:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to 'Ali
3871,"Narrated Umm Salamah:""The Prophet (ﷺ) put a garment over Al-Hasan"
3872,"Narrated 'Aishah:""I have not seen anyone closer in conduct"
3873,Narrated Umm Salamah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) called Fatimah on the Day of the Conquest (of Makkah) and he spoke to her
3874,"Narrated Jumai' bin 'Umair At-Taimi:""I entered along with my uncle upon 'Aishah and she was asked: 'Who among people was the most beloved to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?' She said: 'Fatimah.' So it was said: 'From the men?' She said: 'Her husband"
3875,"Narrated 'Aishah:""I was not jealous of any wife of the Prophet (ﷺ) as I was jealous of Khadijah"
3876,"Narrated 'Aishah:""I did not envy any woman as I envied Khadijah - and the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not marry me except after she had died - that was because the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave her glad tidings of a house in Paradise made of Qasab"
3877,"Narrated 'Ali bin Abi Talib:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The best of its women is Khadijah bint Khuwailid"
3878,"Narrated Anas [may Allah be pleased with him]:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Sufficient for you among the women of mankind are Mariam bint 'Imran"
3879,"Narrated 'Aishah:""The people used to give their gifts [to the Prophet (ﷺ)] on 'Aishah's day."" She said: ""So my companions gathered with Umm Salamah and they said 'O Umm Salamah! The people give their gifts on 'Aishah's day"
3880,Narrated 'Aishah:that Jibril came to the Prophet (ﷺ) with her image upon a piece of green silk cloth
3881,"Narrated 'Aishah [may Allah be pleased with her]:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""O 'Aishah! Here is Jibril and he is giving Salam to you."" She said: ""I said: 'And upon him be peace and the mercy of Allah"
3882,"Narrated 'Aishah:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: 'Indeed Jibril gives his Salam to you.' So I said: 'And upon him be peace and Allah's Mercy [and His blessings]"
3883,"Narrated Abu Musa:""Never was a Hadith unclear to us - the Companions of the Messenger of Allah - and we asked 'Aishah"
3884,"Narrated Musa bin Talhah:""I have not seen anyone clearer (in speech) than 'Aishah"
3885,"Narrated 'Amr bin Al-'As:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) appointed him as a leader of the army of Dhatis-Salasil. He said: ""So I went to him and said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Who is the most beloved to you among the people?' He said: ''Aishah.' I said: 'From the men?' He said: 'Her father"
3886,"Narrated 'Amr bin Al-'As:that he said to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ): ""Who is the most beloved of the people to you?"" He said: ""'Aishah."" He said: ""From the men?"" He said: ""Her farther"
3887,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The virtue of 'Aishah over women is like the virtue of Tharid over all other foods"
3888,"Narrated 'Amr bin Ghalib:that a man spoke negatively of 'Aishah before 'Ammar bin Yasir so he said: ""Be gone as one despicable and rejected! Do you insult the beloved of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?"
3889,"Narrated 'Ammar bin Yasir:""She is his wife in the world and in the Hereafter."" - meaning: 'Aishah [may Allah be pleased with her]"
3890,"Narrated Anas [May Allah be pleased with him]:""It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Who is the most beloved of the people to you?' He said: ''Aishah.' It was said: 'From the men?' He said: 'Her father"
3891,"Narrated 'Ikrimah:""After Salat As-Subh"
3892,"Narrated Safiyyah bint Huyai:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered upon me and some words had reached me from Hafsah and 'Aishah. So I mentioned it to him. So he said: 'Why did you not say: ""And how are you two better than me"
3893,Narrated Umm Salamah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) called for Fatimah in the Year of the Conquest to speak to her
3894,"Narrated Anas:said: ""It reached Safiyyah that Hafsah said: 'The daughter of a Jew' so she wept. Then the Prophet (ﷺ) entered upon her while she was crying"
3895,"Narrated 'Aishah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The best of you is the best to his wives"
3896,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""No one should convey to me anything regarding any of my Companions"
3897,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""No one should convey to me anything regarding anyone"
3898,"Narrated Ubayy bin Ka'b:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to him: ""Indeed Allah has ordered me to recite the Qur'an to you."" So he recited to him: ""Those who disbelieved were not going to... (98:1) and he recited in it: ""Indeed the religion with Allah is that which is Hanafiyyah"
3899,"Narrated Ubayy bin Ka'b:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""If it were not for the Hijrah"
3900,Narrated Shu'bah:from 'Adi bin Thabit
3901,"Narrated Anas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gathered a group of people from the Ansar and said: ""Come"
3902,Zaid bin Arqam wrote to Anas bin Malik
3903,"Narrated Abu Talhah:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: 'Convey my Salam to your people"
3904,"Narrated Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed my elite"
3905,"Narrated Sa'd:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever wishes to humiliate the Quraish then Allah will humiliate him"
3906,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""The Prophet (ﷺ) said to me: 'A man who believes in Allah and the Last Day does not hate the Ansar"
3907,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The Ansar are my close ones and my elite. Indeed the people shall increase and they shall dwindle"
3908,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""O Allah! You made the first of the Quraish taste punishment"
3909,"Narrated Anas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""O Allah forgive the Ansar and the children of the Ansar"
3910,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Shall I inform you of the best houses of the Ansar"
3911,"Narrated Abu Usaid As-Sa'idi:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The Best houses of the Ansar are the houses of Banu An-Najjar"
3912,"Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The best house of the Ansar is Banu An-Najjar"
3913,"Narrated Jabir [bin 'Abdullah]:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The best of the Ansar are Banu 'Abdul-Ashhal"
3914,"Narrated 'Ali bin Abi Talib:""We departed with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) until he was at Harrah As-Suqya which belonged to Sa'd bin Abi Waqqas. So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Bring me water for Wudu.' So he performed Wudu"
3915,"Narrated 'Ali bin Abi Talib and Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whatever is between my house and my Minbar is a garden from the gardens of Paradise"
3916,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""What is between my house and my Minbar is a garden from the gardens of Paradise."" And with this chain"
3917,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever is able to die in Al-Madinah"
3918,Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that a freed a slave girl of his came to him
3919,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The last of the cities of Islam to be destroyed is Al-Madinah"
3920,Narrated Jabir:that a Bedouin gave the pledge to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) for Islam
3921,"Narrated Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab:that Abu Hurairah used to say: ""If I saw hyenas roaming in Al-Madinah"
3922,"Narrated Anas bin Malik:that (mount) Uhud appeared to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) so he said: ""This mountain loves us and we love it. O Allah! Indeed Ibrahim made Makkah sacred"
3923,"Narrated Jarir bin 'Abdullah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed Allah has revealed to me that: Whichever of these three places you go to will be the place of your emigration: Al-Madinah"
3924,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""No one is patient with the difficulties and hardships of Al-Madinah"
3925,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin 'Adi bin Hamra [Az-Zuhri]:""I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) standing at Al-Hazwarah"
3926,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said about Makkah: ""How sweet of a land you are and how dear you are to me"
3927,"Narrated Salman:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said to me: 'O Salman! Do not detest me and thereby leave your religion.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! How could I detest you while Allah guided us by you.' He said: 'You will detest the Arabs and thereby detest me"
3928,"Narrated 'Uthman bin 'Affan:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever cheats the Arabs"
3929,"Narrated Muhammad bin Abi Razin:that his mother said: ""If someone died from the Arabs it would be hard upon Umm Al-Harir so it was said to her: 'We see that if a man from the Arabs dies it is hard upon you.' She said: 'I heard my Mawla say that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""From the (signs of) coming of the Hour is the destruction of the Arabs."" Muhammad bin Abi Razin said: ""And her Mawla was Talhah bin Malik"
3930,"Narrated Umm Sharik:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The people will flee from the Dajjal such that they will go to the mountains."" Umm Sharik said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Where will the Arabs be that day?"" He said: ""They will be few"
3931,"Narrated Samurah bin Jundab:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Sam was the father of Arabs"
3932,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:""Al-'Ajam (non-Arabs) were mentioned before the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) so the Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'I am supported more by them"
3933,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:""We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when Surat Al-Jumu'ah was revealed"
3934,"Narrated Zaid bin Thabit [may Allah be pleased with him]:that the Prophet (ﷺ) looked towards Yemen and said: ""O Allah direct their hearts and bless us in our Sa' and our Mudd"
3935,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The people of Yemen have come to you. They are weaker in heart and softer in understanding"
3936,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Leadership is among the Quraish"
3937,"Narrated Anas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Al-Azd is Allah's lion upon the earth"
3938,"Narrated Anas:""If we are not from Al-Azd then we are not from the people"
3939,Narrated Mina
3941,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Aslam"
3942,"Narrated Jabir:""They said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Thaqif are razing us with their arrows"
3943,"Narrated 'Imran bin Husain:""The Prophet (ﷺ) died while he was having trouble with three tribes: Thaqif"
3944,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""In Thaqif there is a liar and a destroyer"
3945,Narrated Abu Hurairah:that a Bedouin gave a young female camel as a gift to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)
3946,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:""A man from Banu Fazarah gave a gift to the Prophet (ﷺ) of she-camel from his camels which they had taken at Al-Ghabah. So he reciprocated for it with something in return"
3947,"Narrated 'Amir bin Abi 'Amir Al-Ash'ari:from his father who said: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Blessed are the tribes of Al-Asad and Al-Ash'arun"
3948,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Aslam"
3949,"Narrated 'Abdullah bin Dinar:similar to Shu'bah (#3948) and he added: ""And 'Usayyah has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger"
3950,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""By the One in Whose Hand is Muhammad's soul! Ghifar"
3951,"Narrated 'Imran bin Husain:that a group from Banu Tamim came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) so he said: ""Have glad tidings O Banu Tamim."" They said: ""You have given us glad tidings"
3952,"Narrated Abu Bakrah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Aslam"
3953,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""O Allah bless us in our Sham! O Allah bless us in our Yemen."" They said: ""And in our Najd"" He said: ""O Allah bless us in our Sham and bless us in our Yemen."" They said: ""And in our Najd"" He said: ""Earthquakes are there"
3954,"Narrated Zaid bin Thabit:""We were with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) collecting the Qur'an on pieces of cloth"
3955,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""People should stop boasting about their fathers who have died"
3956,"Narrated Abu Hurairah [may Allah be pleased with him]:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Allah has removed the pride of Jahiliyyah from you and boasting about lineage. (A person is either) a pious believer or a miserable sinner"
